WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.350
Skin lightening is about power.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:11.480
It's an expression of power

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.790
and so people who lighten their skin

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:16.030
are doing this because

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:19.790
they are responding to a power dynamic

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:23.400
that exists in their particular society.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.640
In many parts of the world, lighter skin

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.563
is considered to be more
beautiful than darker skin.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:30.720
It's a beauty standard

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.660
that's been around for hundreds of years.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.310
Lighter skin has been associated
with power and privilege,

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:40.000
and the beauty industry has been profiting

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.060
selling skin lightening creams and soaps

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.960
which are popular across Asia,
Africa and the Caribbean.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.280
By 2027, the global
market for skin lighteners

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.843
is estimated to reach over $12 billion.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:56.420
Skin whitening is
definitely a huge business.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:59.280
The patients look forward to have

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.900
a much fairer or a whiter skin,

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.173
and they could go to any
lengths to achieve that.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:22.510
The history of skin lightening
here in the United States.

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:24.710
It actually begins with white women.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:27.350
White women here would use
skin lightening products

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.740
because they were trying
to emulate beauty standards

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:34.200
and beauty practices that
were circulating in Europe.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.480
And then around the Jim Crow era,

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.040
what we see is skin lightening products

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.420
being used and sold and circulated

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.547
within the African-American community.

00:01:44.547 --> 00:01:49.140
Black women would use this partly because

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:53.570
it would be a survival
strategy essentially.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.610
The lighter your skin was

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:58.730
the more access to
resources you would have.

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:02.350
And so this is what made

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:05.120
skin lightening products in part popular

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.790
among more communities of color.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:08.840
The idea was that

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:12.070
if you were trying to
emulate the people in power,

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.170
you were seen as more civilized,

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.180
you were seen as cleaner,

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:19.590
and therefore that would give
you access to certain things.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.300
It would allow you upward mobility,

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.623
upward class mobility, et cetera.

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:30.550
When I was a kid,

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.090
I could say I was one shade

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.063
more darker than my sister.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.270
And we both went to the same school.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:41.430
Everybody used to be a
little surprised when

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.720
I told them she was my sister.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.170
So they said, how is there
such a huge difference

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:47.810
in your skin color?

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.370
So I always had this,

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:52.240
but there was no pressure
from my family members.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.530
But friends and classmates

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.880
definitely did question
me about my skin color

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.460
once upon a time.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.560
In Asia, the practice of skin whitening

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.280
is related to colorism,

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.280
a looks-based discrimination
that occurs within racial

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.030
or ethnic groups.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:09.980
And in India, a part of everyday life.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.930
Individuals who have fairer
skin are more acceptable

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:18.450
when it comes to career or marriage.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.790
If you also go to the matrimonial columns

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.760
in the newspapers or magazines,

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.890
they say, I look for a fairer bride,

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:28.770
or there are women who
look for a fairer groom.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.530
So it's equal.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.280
The desire to have a fairer skin

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.393
is deep-seated in Indian population.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.670
Most experts agree

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.910
that colorism bled into
India's caste system

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.300
where darker skin has
since become associated

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.100
with Indians at the lowest levels

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.660
of the social hierarchy,
who do manual labor.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:52.160
Historians are undecided about the origins

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:53.950
of this color prejudice.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:56.130
While some point to ancient migrations

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.450
by Indo-Europeans, Arabs and Persians,

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.910
all of whom had strikingly
lighter colored skin

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.720
than local inhabitants.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.010
Others note the more recent colonial rule

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:06.843
of the British empire.

00:04:06.843 --> 00:04:07.676
The Britishers ruled us for
about roughly 200 years.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:15.570
The Indians were kind
of treated very badly,

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:17.010
or they were slaves.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:19.400
They worked for the Britishers
for many, many years.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.570
So they look forward to the British skin

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.890
and they thought that the British skin

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:28.090
was acceptable because there were fairer.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:29.670
Asia is the biggest market

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:31.440
for skin lightening products.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.630
The World Health Organization
found the 40% of women

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:37.760
they asked in China, India
and other Asian countries,

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:39.463
said they regularly use them.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.170
In India, skin lightening

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.480
is a multi-million-dollar industry.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:47.880
Around 80% of skin
moisturizers on the market

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.810
are for skin whitening.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.390
The most widely used was Fair &amp; Lovely.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:55.260
It earns more than $500 million each year

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.670
for Unilever from India alone.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:04:59.760
So I used to see the product Fair &amp; Lovely

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.210
even while I was a kid.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:04.330
So it's about 45 years old.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.020
It is quite popular and it's manufactured

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:09.362
by a company called
Hindustan Unilever limited.

00:05:09.362 --> 00:05:12.670
And it's a booming business.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:14.740
Due to global public pressure on brands

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:17.610
following the 2020 George Floyd protests,

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.430
the Indian affiliate of Unilever

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.920
changed the name to Glow &amp; Lovely.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.437
In a statement the company said,

00:05:23.437 --> 00:05:25.150
"We recognize the use of words,

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.480
'fair', 'white' and 'light'

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:28.830
suggests a singular ideal of beauty

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:30.080
that we don't think is right,

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.617
and we want to address this."

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.560
The Indian government
has proposed jail terms

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.683
and fines for advertisements
which promote skin whitening.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.460
But that hasn't stopped many Indians

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.793
obsessed with lighter skin
buying and using these products.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.960
Something like this has been going on

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:50.690
in our societies for so long.

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:53.500
We discriminate people
based on their skin color

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.790
and no one's saying anything about it.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.790
You know, when you see the
way it affects children,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.730
it affects women, it affects men,

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:02.433
and they grow with that
sense of insecurity.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.550
It's like a journey we've
been on this toxic belief,

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.260
where it started with culture,

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.860
it started with social hierarchies

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.090
and the media keeps endorsing it.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.910
Companies they may not have initiated it,

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:17.570
but by endorsing it, by selling products

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:19.850
through advertisements that say that

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:21.720
you can be whiter in seven days

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:24.250
or white is better, if you're fairer,

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.020
you'll be more successful too.

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:28.650
The thing is they're using the insecurity

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:32.300
that colorism has bred
to sell their product.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:36.950
So you're kind of making money
off people's insecurities.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:39.673
And then we just lived with
it and it's become normal.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:43.890
Apart from using whitening product,

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:45.920
some people go even further,

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.560
receiving cosmetic procedures

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.803
like chemical peels or laser treatment.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:53.670
In recent years, an
antioxidant called glutathione

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:55.133
is gaining popularity.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.280
While it's available to take orally,

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.550
many consumers believe injecting the drug

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:03.340
is faster and more effective
for skin whitening,

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.503
but this hasn't been
scientifically proven.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:08.870
If they have a medical condition,

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:10.000
yes, I will do it.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.827
But if they just want to achieve
a skin whitening treatment,

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:18.550
I would refuse to do that for them

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:23.550
because the safety and efficacy
of the drug glutathione

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:25.843
is not well established.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.810
Glutathione is produced naturally

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:30.150
in the human liver.

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:32.310
In India, oral glutathione is approved

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.370
for treating skin conditions
and for skin whitening.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:38.020
But intravenous and
intramuscular glutathione

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.470
is only approved to
treat medical conditions

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:42.563
like the side effects of chemotherapy.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:46.150
There are very few clinical trials.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:49.230
There are certain drawbacks
to those studies because

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:50.370
those studies were done

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:52.550
on a very limited number of subjects.

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.530
Also, the patients were not followed up

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:56.965
for a long term or a long period.

00:07:56.965 --> 00:07:59.700
There are practitioners who do use it,

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:01.900
but it's an off-label indication.

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:05.200
But what has been observed is that

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:09.450
it's a very subjective
opinion from the patient

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:14.060
in terms of how much of skin lightening

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:16.430
they have been able to
achieve with the treatment.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:20.520
So it's not necessary
that if you administer

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.040
the infusion in ten patients,

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:23.900
all of the ten patients are going

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:25.923
to observe the same change.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:29.170
Due to a lack of research and regulations,

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:31.070
clinics make up their own protocols

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.580
and set their own prices,

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.623
ranging from $50 to $70 per injection.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.530
In the Philippines, almost
400 years of Spanish

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:44.410
and then American colonial rule

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:47.290
helped to reinforce the
notion of beauty as white.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:50.730
And so today, glutathione is
becoming a popular alternative

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.960
to traditional lightening products.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:56.290
When we look at a place
like the Philippines,

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:59.570
people there will use
skin lightening products

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:03.070
because they're trying to emulate

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:04.590
those who are in power;

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:07.520
they're trying to emulate
things that they see on TV.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:10.530
And when you watch, for
example, Philippine TV,

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:14.550
it's inundated with actors
and actresses and performers

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:17.350
who are typically light-skinned.

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:19.490
When you look at the
Philippine government,

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:24.157
many politicians are either
mixed race or light-skinned.

00:09:33.567 --> 00:09:35.730
Marjorie Taguiling owns a beauty salon

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:38.420
in downtown Manila which
offers beauty services

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:40.873
including glutathione
drips for skin whitening.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.470
The country's Food and Drug Administration

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:04.130
has warned against the use
of injectable glutathione

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:05.450
for skin whitening,

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.760
flagging its toxic effects on the liver,

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:10.270
kidneys and nervous system.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:13.050
But many big medical groups
and small beauty salons

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:17.313
still provided with a price
tag of up to $120 per session.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:41.570
Some beauty salons or moonlighting nurses

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:43.850
even offer injections at home.

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:47.160
But glutathione drips can
also be bought easily online.

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.200
So some take it into their own hands,

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.190
following online tutorials.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:53.730
So for tonight's video,

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:57.240
I'm gonna show you how to inject yourself

00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:58.913
with glutathione.

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:21.990
I would say that is unacceptable

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:25.470
because sometimes if it is
injected in the wrong manner

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:28.210
or if it is injected in a huge dose,

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:31.500
it can cause severe allergic reactions.

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:35.170
Sometimes it can be a
casualty or an emergency.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:39.100
These videos should be totally prohibited

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.853
on social media platforms.

00:13:17.626 --> 00:13:19.530
I think it's an issue of access.

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:23.890
The more available a certain process is

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:27.510
the more people are going
to be curious about it.

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:31.560
These more advanced processes,

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:36.160
what they do is they
create more legitimacy

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:38.290
for the practice,

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:41.510
but at no point do we step back and say,

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:43.989
why is this necessary to begin with?

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:02.820
While some are still
doing whatever it takes

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:04.030
to become lighter,

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.650
others are beginning to
embrace their own skin.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.580
And awareness of color discrimination

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:10.749
has increased in recent years.

00:14:10.749 --> 00:14:12.790
India's Got Color.

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:15.380
In India, advocacy group Dark is Beautiful

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:18.940
has been organizing workshops
and events to fight colorism.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:21.900
What needs to happen is
change both within culture

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:26.248
as well as change from
these external endorsements.

00:14:26.248 --> 00:14:30.420
And cosmetic brands and
businesses have a responsibility,

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:34.440
it's not about people
want it, and so we do it.

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:37.620
This is not like some problem
that we can fix overnight.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.430
It takes several such movements,

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:41.420
several such campaigns like ours,

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:43.490
like the Dark is Beautiful campaign.

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:45.820
And so it's gonna take some time

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.433
before we can feel the change.

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:53.120
We have to ground change in structures.

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:56.380
So we need to see major
reforms in education,

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.810
we need to see major
reforms in government,

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:02.230
and we need to see major
reforms in media representation.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:04.540
And not just aesthetic representation,

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:08.550
it's not enough to cast
darker-skinned people on TV

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:11.800
and think yeah, people are
going to love their skin.

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:15.250
It's about how we're
represented in government

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:19.590
and taking away historical
governmental policies

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:24.280
that were created to
subjugate people of color,

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:27.383
that were created to subjugate
darker-skinned people.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:31.735
We spend a lot of time
grooming our outside, right?

00:15:31.735 --> 00:15:34.780
We dress up, we want to be presentable,

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:36.840
we dress a certain way.

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:41.840
So I think what really will
help us is mental grooming,

00:15:42.530 --> 00:15:46.860
to keep telling ourselves
every day that you are enough,

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:48.560
you are enough just the way you are

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:50.446
and every skin color is beautiful.

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:56.570
On the next episode of
Business of Beauty...

00:15:56.570 --> 00:15:59.670
Istanbul is arguably the
world's most popular city

00:15:59.670 --> 00:16:02.030
to get hair transplant treatment.

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:04.150
Before Covid hit, it's estimated that

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.870
half a million people came here every year

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:09.140
in the hopes of regaining their hair.

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:11.070
In no small part because of the quality

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:12.490
of the work being offered

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:13.990
and the price it's offered at.

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:17.880
But it's a lightly regulated industry

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:21.050
and with hundreds of clinics
competing against each other,

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:23.500
the pressure is on to increase operations

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.073
and cut prices even further.

